WEBVTT

00:03:29.708 --> 00:03:31.768
but it's actually a very safe submersible.

00:03:31.792 --> 00:03:34.268
I like to say I don't trust
a lot of things in life,

00:03:34.292 --> 00:03:36.101
but I do trust titanium, I trust math

00:03:36.125 --> 00:03:38.184
and I trust finite element analysis,

00:03:38.208 --> 00:03:39.518
which is how you figure out

00:03:39.542 --> 00:03:41.601
whether or not
things like this can survive

00:03:41.625 --> 00:03:43.768
these extraordinary
pressures and conditions.

00:03:43.792 --> 00:03:46.934
DB: And that sphere
is so perfectly machined, right?

00:03:46.958 --> 00:03:48.934
This is a truly unique craft.

00:03:48.958 --> 00:03:50.434
VV: That was the real trick --

00:03:50.458 --> 00:03:52.309
is actually building a titanium sphere

00:03:52.333 --> 00:03:55.476
that was accurate
to within .1 percent of machine.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:57.059
Titanium is a hard metal to work

00:03:57.083 --> 00:03:59.143
and a lot of people
haven't figured it out,

00:03:59.167 --> 00:04:00.518
but we were very fortunate.